From: jorink <maxjorink@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vim: Enter, arrows and Tab work in normal mode

In normal mode every key with a character went to the vim handler, and
Enter has one (\r), so it was swallowed: an item could only be picked
after `i`. Keys that are not plain characters (BM_KEY_UNICODE) now fall
through to the normal handling, like in insert mode.
---
diff --git a/lib/vim.c b/lib/vim.c
index b61948c..f5bbcfe 100644
--- a/lib/vim.c
+++ b/lib/vim.c
@@ -211,6 +211,9 @@ enum bm_vim_code bm_vim_key_press(struct bm_menu *menu, enum bm_key key, uint32_
             return BM_VIM_CONSUME;
         }
 
+        // Enter, arrows, Tab etc. act as in insert mode; only characters are vim keys
+        if(key != BM_KEY_UNICODE) return BM_VIM_IGNORE;
+
         if(unicode == 0 || unicode > 128) return BM_VIM_IGNORE;
 
         if(menu->vim_last_key == 0) return vim_on_first_key(menu, unicode, item_count, items_displayed);
